Z||000005||Joe Torma||08-28-2001||10:45 AM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Rich86GT:<BR><B>Oops.  <P>White 1986 Fiero GT, 2.8L V6, 5 speed, 142,000 miles with 32,000 on rebuilt engine.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>That helps...You can't select ANY gear from messing with the arms on the trans? Push in, pull out, turn--nothing???<BR>Must have busted some selector arms inside the trans.  Whattya hammering through the gears?  Never heard of this one.<P>Joe<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/simplesig.gif">  <p>[This message has been edited by Joe Torma (edited 08-28-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||fldevel||08-28-2001||02:31 PM||||my 4 speed did that when i found out it had somehow knocked a hole in the bottom of my tranny and all the fluid had leaked out .. try checking and making sure there is oil in there ||||reg||1
Z||000007||Rich86GT||08-28-2001||08:01 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Joe Torma:<BR><B>  That helps...You can't select ANY gear from messing with the arms on the trans? Push in, pull out, turn--nothing???<BR>Must have busted some selector arms inside the trans.  Whattya hammering through the gears?  Never heard of this one.<P>Joe<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Doesn't matter if you push in, pull out, or turn (any combination) on the transmission levers, it never engages.  There's oil in thar too.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000008||Rich86GT||10-03-2001||08:22 PM||||After removing the transmission, having it rebuilt, installing a new clutch kit, and reinstalling the transmission, it works great!!!!  One of the selector levers inside the transmission bent.<BR>||||reg||7
